- How would you extend to handle parallel resources or varying durations per edge?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests mastery of graph algorithms, state expansion techniques, and path reconstruction under constraints.

## Key Concepts
- Dijkstra's algorithm on expanded state space (node, used)
- Edge relaxation with and without discount application
- Path reconstruction across state transitions

## Code Example
```javascript
function shortestWithDiscounts(n, edges, s, t, K) {
  const adj = Array.from({length: n}, ()=>[]);
  for(const [u,v,w] of edges){ adj[u].push([v,w]); }
  const INF = Number.POSITIVE_INFINITY;
  const dist = Array.from({length: n}, ()=> Array(K+1).fill(INF));
  const prev = Array.from({length: n}, ()=> Array(K+1).fill(null));

  const pq = new MinHeap();
  dist[s][0] = 0;
  pq.insert([s,0,0]); // [node, used, distance]

  while(!pq.isEmpty()){
    const [u,used,d] = pq.extractMin();
    if(d > dist[u][used]) continue;
    if(u === t) break;

    for(const [v,w] of adj[u]){
      // Without discount
      if(d + w < dist[v][used]){
        dist[v][used] = d + w;
        prev[v][used] = [u,used];
        pq.insert([v,used,d+w]);
      }
      // With discount if available
      if(used < K && d < dist[v][used+1]){
        dist[v][used+1] = d;
        prev[v][used+1] = [u,used];
        pq.insert([v,used+1,d]);
      }
    }
  }

  // Find optimal state at target
  let minDist = INF, minUsed = -1;
  for(let k=0;k<=K;k++){
    if(dist[t][k] < minDist){
      minDist = dist[t][k];
      minUsed = k;
    }
  }

  // Path reconstruction
  const path = [];
  let curr = [t,minUsed];
  while(curr && prev[curr[0]][curr[1]]){
    path.unshift(curr[0]);
    curr = prev[curr[0]][curr[1]];
  }
  if(curr[0] === s) path.unshift(s);

  return {distance: minDist, path};
}
```

## Edge Cases
- Unreachable target: return INF distance
- K=0: reduces to standard Dijkstra
- K larger than path length: effectively unlimited discounts
- Multiple optimal states: choose minimal used count

## Why This Is Asked
This tests building a Trie and adding an autocomplete-style suggest method, a common real-world need.

## Key Concepts
- Trie nodes with 26 children; end-of-word markers; storing full word for suggestions
- Lexicographic DFS for deterministic suggestions
- Complexity and memory trade-offs; edge cases like no matches

## Code Example
```javascript
class TrieNode {
  constructor(){ this.children = new Map(); this.isWord=false; this.word=null }
}
class Trie {
  constructor(){ this.root=new TrieNode(); }
  insert(word){ let n=this.root; for (let ch of word){ if(!n.children.has(ch)) n.children.set(ch,new TrieNode()); n=n.children.get(ch); } n.isWord=true; n.word=word; }
  search(word){ let n=this.root; for(let ch of word){ if(!n.children.has(ch)) return false; n=n.children.get(ch); } return n.isWord; }
  startsWith(prefix){ let n=this.root; for(let ch of prefix){ if(!n.children.has(ch)) return false; n=n.children.get(ch); } return true; }
  suggest(prefix, limit){ let n=this.root; for(let ch of prefix){ if(!n.children.has(ch)) return []; n=n.children.get(ch); }
    const res=[];
    const dfs=(cur, path)=>{ if(res.length>=limit) return; if(cur.isWord) res.push(prefix+path); const keys=Array.from(cur.children.keys()).sort(); for(let c of keys){ dfs(cur.children.get(c), path+c); } };
    dfs(n, '');
    return res;
  }
}
```

